images: v1 6080 bytes, v2 6280 bytes (16-byte header + payload + 64-byte Ed25519 signature)
1 good update:        write slot B; mark pending; trial boot v2; confirm v2; boot v2; -> runs v2, after reboot v2
2 wrong signature:    write slot B; mark pending; REFUSED new image (signature, damage or downgrade); boot v1; -> runs v1
3 never confirmed:    write slot B; mark pending; trial boot v2; revert (new image never confirmed); boot v1; -> runs v2, then v1
4 downgrade to v1:    write slot A; mark pending; REFUSED new image (signature, damage or downgrade); boot v2; -> runs v2
A/B slots   update = 29 flash operations; power cut at each one in turn:
            still on v1: 29, on v2: 0, BRICKED: 0
single slot update = 27 flash operations; power cut at each one in turn:
            still on v1: 0, on v2: 0, BRICKED: 27
H4 checks PASS (wrong signature refused; power loss never bricks A/B)
